    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d590">

                <pb facs="0489" n="477" xml:id="pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/6363: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-17T14:00:00+02:00">August 17, 1942—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 17—1:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1116. As I now have informal assurances from Foreign Office here that it knows
                    and approves of the separate negotiations, I believe their discussion with
                    Embassy in Washington inadvisable. Department’s 738, August 14, 7 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
